OL,3,GNEWSAMinister apologises over minimum
OL,4,Awage comments
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe minister for sustainable economic
OL,7,Fdevelopment has apologised for
OL,8,Fcommenting about the minimum wage
OL,9,Fwithout discussing it with colleagues
OL,10,Ffirst.
OL,12,FDeputy Gerald Voisin said he was not
OL,13,Fcalling for the abolition of the
OL,14,Fminimum wage  in a letter he wrote to a
OL,15,Fnewspaper in which he said was
OL,16,F"strangling our economy".
OL,18,FHe said he had wanted to "raise points"
OL,19,Fabout the wage which he felt "had been
OL,20,Flacking".
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
